menu "PlantHub Storage"

config PLANTHUB_HISTORY_RAW_CAP
    int "Raw-tier history ring capacity (samples per plant)"
    default 1344 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C5
    default 2880
    help
        Number of raw-tier storage_rec_t slots kept per plant, ring-buffer
        style (oldest overwritten first). Each ring file is a fixed-size
        preallocation of this many 22-byte records plus a small header, so
        this directly sizes the "storage" littlefs partition's raw-history
        footprint per plant.

        The ESP32-C5 default is lower than C3's because its "storage"
        partition is half the size (384K vs 768K -- see partitions_c5.csv,
        which trades storage space for bigger OTA app slots and dual-band
        WiFi/Zigbee headroom). Lower only for a custom partition table with
        even less "storage" space; raising it risks exhausting the
        partition once enough plants are actively sampled.

config PLANTHUB_HISTORY_HOURLY_CAP
    int "Hourly-tier history ring capacity (samples per plant)"
    default 720
    help
        Number of hourly-aggregated storage_rec_t slots kept per plant
        (720 hours = 30 days at one bucket/hour). Same ring-buffer
        semantics and per-plant file as the raw tier, just coarser.

endmenu
